                <pb facs="0156" n="834" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg834"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Affidavit of Solon A. Perkins.</hi></head>
                <p>I, Solon A. Perkins, 1st lieutenant commanding the 3d unattached company of
                    Massachusetts cavalry, on oath depose and say, that I had command of the cavalry
                    attached to the command of Colonel Stephen Thomas on the expedition of Colonel
                    Thomas on the days of the 28th, 29th and 30th of August, A. D. 1862; that I have
                    carefully read the deposition of Colonel Thomas, and am able to state that the
                    history of said expedition, and of the conduct of the officers and men in
                    reference to François Bougére and his property, is correct and true.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">SOLON A. PERKINS, 1<hi rendition="#italic">st Lieut.
                        Com’dg</hi> 3<hi rendition="#italic">d unattached company Massachusetts
                        Cavalry.</hi></p>
                <p>Subscribed and sworn to before me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BION BRADBURY, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Commissioner.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
